<title>SOUTH AFRICA: TABLE - SEARDEL YR SHR DIPS, DIV STEADY.</title>
<headline>TABLE - SEARDEL YR SHR DIPS, DIV STEADY.</headline>
<dateline>CAPE TOWN 1997-08-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Yr ended June 30, 1997</p>
<p>		 (million of rand unless indicated)</p>
<p>Shr</p>
<p>    - headline (cts)	26.5     vs  45.5</p>
<p>    - after excepts (cts) 29.3     vs  47.6</p>
<p>    Final div (cts)	  5.25    making 9.25 vs  9.25</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   31.4     vs  49.7</p>
<p>    Before tax income     94.2     vs 136.0</p>
<p>    After tax income	74.5     vs  94.7</p>
<p>    Turnover		2,876.4    vs 2,714.7</p>
<p>Div payable Nov 21</p>
<p>on register Nov 7</p>
<p>Full name: Seardel Investment Corporation Ltd</p>
<p>NOTE: The group said local retailing trade was slowly improving but margins still needed to be improved. Exports to the U.S. were expected to rise after cuts in U.S. import duties and the group expected to benefit from restructuring over the last year</p>
<p>It said it planned to move its head office as part of is cost cutting drive and repeated its cautionary on a possible management buy-out.</p>
<p>-- Cape Town newsroom +27 21 25-2238</p>
